READING
  1. Direct Freiman small-doubling is too strong for the third pocket:
     KPS relation-covered examples have |S+S| well above 3k-4, so they are not
     automatically one-dimensional GAP rows by the elementary 3k-4 window.
  2. The useful condition is relation coverage plus shell location.  Shifted AP
     has maximal additive energy but zero visible folds; AP has the same energy
     and many observer-coupled folds.  Energy without the summand-node address
     is a decoy.
  3. Addition supplies candidate denominators C in S+S; multiplication tests
     clearance by divisibility C|w.  Positive/negative signs in a relation say
     whether the relation is balanced (even scalar, translation-invariant) or
     observer-coupled (odd marked, translation-sensitive).
  4. The proof target should be a relation-hypergraph regularity lemma:
     either a dissociated stranger peels, or the small-relation hypergraph has
     enough low visible/hidden summand-shell payload that the signed reciprocal
     tail can be channelized before absolute values.

